From: AztecBot <tech@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:40:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(p2p,aztec-nr): reject and never emit private logs with
 non-zero padding

The tx base rollup rejects any private log whose fields beyond its emitted length are not zero, because the tx hash commits to all PRIVATE_LOG_SIZE_IN_FIELDS fields while only the emitted prefix is published.

- p2p: DataTxValidator rejects such a tx at the mempool with TX_ERROR_PRIVATE_LOG_PADDING, so a sequencer never builds a block it cannot prove.
- stdlib: PrivateLog.hasZeroPadding() carries the check.
- aztec-nr: emit_raw_note_log_unsafe copies only the live prefix of the BoundedVec, so a caller that truncated or popped the vector cannot leak stale storage into the padding.

